\description{
\code{RSConcreteSet} is the internal storage adapter shared by \link{RSSet} and
\link{RSMutableSet}. It lazily owns an external pointer to a C++ \code{NativeSet} and
keeps all Rcpp bridge calls out of the public set classes.

This class provides storage semantics only. It does not inherit from
\link{RSObject}, copy inserted objects, translate \code{NULL}, or impose mutable versus
immutable behavior. Objects are retained by the native storage and equality
is determined by their \code{hash()} and \code{isEqual()} methods.

The set operations mutate the receiver. They correspond to the operations
provided by Foundation's mutable set: union, intersection, and subtraction.
}
\section{Methods}{

\itemize{
\item \code{duplicate()} returns an independent shallow copy of the native table.
\item \code{add(item)} inserts an item when no equal member exists.
\item \code{member(item)} returns the stored equal member, or \code{NULL} when absent.
\item \code{contains(item)} reports whether an equal member exists.
\item \code{remove(item)} removes an equal member and reports whether it existed.
\item \code{clear()} removes every member.
\item \code{allObjects()} returns the stored objects in unspecified order.
\item \code{count()} returns the number of members.
\item \code{uniteWith(other)}, \code{intersectWith(other)}, and \code{subtractWith(other)} mutate
this storage using another \code{RSConcreteSet}.
\item \code{contentHash()} returns an order-independent aggregate member hash.
\item \code{prepareForSerialization()} captures a temporary R snapshot used only to
rebuild the native table after deserialization.
}
}

